  "prefLabel": "Env-Wt 511.07 Beach Replenishment Project Classifications",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wt 511.07 Beach Replenishment Project Classifications.\n\n(a) Replenishment of sand on an existing beach shall be a minimum impact project only if all of the following criteria are met:\n\n(1) The beach is an existing legal structure as defined in Env-Wt 102;\n\n(2) No sand is placed below the normal high water line or limits of flowage rights, as applicable;\n\n(3) No work is done in a wetland, watercourse, or PRA, except as provided in Env-Wt 407;\n\n(4) No more than 10 CY of sand is used; and\n\n(5) The beach is not replenished more frequently than once in any 6-year period.\n\n(b) Replenishment of a beach shall be a minor impact project if the project meets the criteria in (a)(1)-(3), above, and either:\n\n(1) The beach is replenished more frequently than once in a 6-year period; or\n\n(2) More than 10 CY of sand but not more than 20 CY of sand will be used.\n\n(c) Replenishment of an existing legal beach shall be a major impact project if the project does not meet the criteria specified in (a) or (b), above.\n\n(d) A beach that is not an existing legal structure shall not be replenished unless an after-the-fact permit is obtained for construction of the beach, which shall be classified as provided in Env-Wt 511.06.\n\nSource. #12805, eff 12-15-19; ss by #13134, eff 10-23-20; ss by #13776, eff 10-13-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wt500.html"
}
